## Provider capacity (which side is scarce)

State which provider is ABUNDANT and which is SCARCE for YOU — this depends on your actual
subscriptions/billing, not on the models, and it is what ROUTING.md's budget rules refer to. For
example:

- **<provider A> (<plan>): ABUNDANT** — use it for bulk / parallel / high-fan-out / low-stakes work.
- **<provider B> (<plan>, metered how): SCARCE** — spend it only on decorrelation (plan review,
  adversarial review of finished work, a contested second opinion), never on volume.

If you have only ONE provider, say so — then the cross-provider routing rules do not apply and you
route by skill within that provider's ladder.

## Environment

Anything machine-specific an agent should know, e.g.:

- Whether this machine runs more than one OS (dual-boot), and what that implies for paths / memory
  dir encodings / file ownership.
